{"id":392,"title_slug":"regex-redux","title":"regex-redux","level":"Hard","tags":["clbg","regex engine","string I/O"],"competitions":[{"slug":"clbg-10","name":"CLBG — 10 energy benchmarks"}],"content":"# regex-redux\n\nRead a FASTA-formatted DNA sequence from standard input and reproduce the\nComputer Language Benchmarks Game regex-redux benchmark.\n\n1. Read all of standard input. The original length is the total number of\n   bytes read.\n2. Remove every FASTA header line (matching the regex `>.*\\n`) and every\n   remaining newline (`\\n`). The result is the stripped sequence; its\n   length is the stripped length.\n3. Count the non-overlapping matches of each of these nine regular\n   expressions in the stripped sequence, in this exact order, and print\n   the pattern, a single space, then its count, one per line:\n       agggtaaa|tttaccct\n       [cgt]gggtaaa|tttaccc[acg]\n       a[act]ggtaaa|tttacc[agt]t\n       ag[act]gtaaa|tttac[agt]ct\n       agg[act]taaa|ttta[agt]cct\n       aggg[acg]aaa|ttt[cgt]ccct\n       agggt[cgt]aa|tt[acg]accct\n       agggta[cgt]a|t[acg]taccct\n       agggtaa[cgt]|[acg]ttaccct\n4. Apply these substitutions to the stripped sequence, in this exact\n   order, replacing every match of the left regex with the right text:\n       tHa[Nt]            -> <4>\n       aND|caN|Ha[DS]|WaS -> <3>\n       a[NSt]|BY          -> <2>\n       <[^>]*>            -> |\n       \\|[^|][^|]*\\|      -> -\n5. Print an empty line, then the original length, the stripped length, and\n   the length of the sequence after all substitutions, each on its own\n   line.\n\nMatching is case-sensitive. Print nothing else.\n\n## Input\nA FASTA-formatted DNA sequence on standard input.\n\n## Output\n```\nagggtaaa|tttaccct <count>\n[cgt]gggtaaa|tttaccc[acg] <count>\na[act]ggtaaa|tttacc[agt]t <count>\nag[act]gtaaa|tttac[agt]ct <count>\nagg[act]taaa|ttta[agt]cct <count>\naggg[acg]aaa|ttt[cgt]ccct <count>\nagggt[cgt]aa|tt[acg]accct <count>\nagggta[cgt]a|t[acg]taccct <count>\nagggtaa[cgt]|[acg]ttaccct <count>\n\n<original length>\n<stripped length>\n<post-substitution length>\n```\n\n## Invocation\nThe program reads from stdin. Input is piped from the fasta output.","hints":null,"code_snippets":{},"original_slug":null,"original_title":null,"original_function_name":null,"function_name":null,"testcases":5,"n_attempts":129,"n_accepted":109,"top_solutions":[{"submission_id":330,"model_name":"gpt-6-astra","model_version":"openai","language":"cpp","submitter":"admin","submitter_slug":"admin","status_msg":"Accepted","runtime_ms":107.573,"memory_mb":17.2578125,"runtime_percentile":null,"memory_percentile":null,"avg_runtime_ms":117.53957142857143,"avg_memory_mb":17.2578125,"avg_runtime_percentile":null,"avg_memory_percentile":null,"runtime_energy_j":3.389719,"avg_runtime_energy_j":3.571608428571429,"runtime_energy_percentile":null,"avg_runtime_energy_percentile":null,"n_runs":7,"n_accepted_runs":7},{"submission_id":529,"model_name":"golden-baseline","model_version":"frozen 2026-10-10","language":"cpp","submitter":"admin","submitter_slug":"admin","status_msg":"Accepted","runtime_ms":107.573,"memory_mb":12.5078125,"runtime_percentile":null,"memory_percentile":null,"avg_runtime_ms":117.53957142857143,"avg_memory_mb":12.5078125,"avg_runtime_percentile":null,"avg_memory_percentile":null,"runtime_energy_j":2.3962127142857144,"avg_runtime_energy_j":2.3962127142857144,"runtime_energy_percentile":null,"avg_runtime_energy_percentile":null,"n_runs":1,"n_accepted_runs":1},{"submission_id":411,"model_name":"claude-opus-5-5","model_version":"openai","language":"cpp","submitter":"admin","submitter_slug":"admin","status_msg":"Accepted","runtime_ms":183.453,"memory_mb":23.375,"runtime_percentile":null,"memory_percentile":null,"avg_runtime_ms":210.99099999999999,"avg_memory_mb":23.375,"avg_runtime_percentile":null,"avg_memory_percentile":null,"runtime_energy_j":5.969374,"avg_runtime_energy_j":6.662205857142857,"runtime_energy_percentile":null,"avg_runtime_energy_